{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507296-is-there-any-disciplines-that-you-stay-away-from-in-player-creation","id":1507296,"title":"Is there any disciplines that you stay away from in player creation?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-03T09:59:51-07:00","id":1507296,"title":"Is there any disciplines that you stay away from in player creation?","content":"Myself I noted that I never had my player characters ever learn blood sorcery even if it would fit the general concept with no real issue. Such as my Malkavian who likes to learn lore of all sorts and never shown an interest in it and looking back at some of my older characters in this game and even VTR I shied away from blood magic in general.<br /> <br /> So is there any disciplines that you generally leave off the table?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T10:44:25-07:00","id":1507297,"title":"","content":"The main clans all have great disciplines. Dementation being an iffy case that I've made a thread somewhere about. Some bloodlines have some troublesome things but most are pretty good. The problems are: Temporis (stupid) , spiritus (obviously someone's pet discipline, really enviable but I'd rather just increase the versatility of Protean) Abombwe (as with spiritus) <br /> I consider mytherceria an Auspex path, for those who'll hunt fae, because otherwise a lot of powers are just better auspex.<br /> <br /> On a related tangent: it's interesting to play a Nosferatu (or Samedi) without obfuscate. Thinking of clever ways to mitigate your weakness without an easy hack from the getgo is fun. Mask of a Thousand faces is a fantastic and fun power I think everyone should strive for, but it's even better to earn it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T11:04:43-07:00","id":1507299,"title":"","content":"Samedia thanatosis is terrible so I avoid it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T17:06:40-07:00","id":1507326,"title":"","content":"Temporis would fit better in a Mage or a Changeling game inhmo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-04-2023, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T17:12:46-07:00","id":1507327,"title":"","content":"I've noticed that I tend to favor the use of the Auspex, Fortitude, Obfuscate, Presence &amp; Protean disciplines with many of my characters with Potence &amp; Celerity a close second. Blood Sorcery &amp; Dominate tend to fall onto the in the seldom used side though my Malkavian has some knowledge of mental manipulation. Though I see him more of a charmer then a tyrant at his worst times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T17:35:18-07:00","id":1507331,"title":"","content":"I find it really depends on the genre of game you are running, which in turn is an extension of your group's interests.<br /> <br /> The common disciplines for a combat junkie group will be very different from the common disciplines for a social focused group. Likewise, a group which focuses on empire building will have a different discipline list from the previous two groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T17:40:07-07:00","id":1507332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507296-is-there-any-disciplines-that-you-stay-away-from-in-player-creation?p=1507331#post1507331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it really depends on the genre of game you are running, which in turn is an extension of your group's interests.<br /> <br /> The common disciplines for a combat junkie group will be very different from the common disciplines for a social focused group. Likewise, a group which focuses on empire building will have a different discipline list from the previous two groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>True the group that my Malkavian is part of are collectors of lore and deep dark secrets and there discipline and skill spread do reflect this with a focus on getting out of danger as quickly as possible.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T17:45:00-07:00","id":1507334,"title":"","content":"In my case, I don't have as much experience with unique clan disciplines, I tend to use more Fortitude, Dominion and Obfuscate; Potence, Celerity and Auspex I only use the first and second levels; Presence, I don't find it very useful, I mean, there was always someone else who preferred to have the social actions so I couldn't even use it anyway, I even like the protean, but you have to be very careful before using it. Blood and necromancy spells have cost issues, so you end up having to specialize in one thing. Temporis is mildly useful, but I think it's only worth it in the long run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T17:48:48-07:00","id":1507335,"title":"","content":"With Presence I like the subtle uses of it instead of the seeming blunt force approach of Dominate. I'd know it can be used discretely by many and I don't have a problem with it, I have never found the right character concept that gelled well with it. I saw my secondary character despite being a monster as a person who can make friends very easily and could make the most haughty Ventrue or Lasombra relax somewhat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-03-2023, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T18:38:31-07:00","id":1507345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507296-is-there-any-disciplines-that-you-stay-away-from-in-player-creation?p=1507332#post1507332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True the group that my Malkavian is part of are collectors of lore and deep dark secrets and there discipline and skill spread do reflect this with a focus on getting out of danger as quickly as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had one game where the coterie was more or less a cyber warfare unit. They would use hacking and drones to destroy their enemy's ability to hold territory or function in the modern world. No one could really fight back because the coterie used an RV to remain mobile and never actually enter the city they laid siege to. The coterie was a mix of Tremere, Nosferatu, and ghouls.<br /> <br /> The Tremere used Path of Technomancy and Path of Conjuration, the Nosferatu was the infiltration specialist and had access to Schrecknet, while the ghouls were day light drivers so the warded RV didn't have to wait for nightfall to get to the next location. The fact that modern camp grounds now have WiFi and local restaurants send complimentary take out menus to the campers is such a wierd thing to me, but very helpful for the game.<br /> <br /> One of our gaming group at the time was a computer security specialist IRL, so I didn't have to rely on movies like Hackers, Swordfish, or Black Hat to give an idea of scale or power for hacking, let alone thamaturgically enhanced hacking.<br /> <br /> That combination broke entire vampire power structures, and no amount of Generation, or dots in disciplines could counter it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T10:50:45-07:00","id":1507416,"title":"","content":"That sounds pretty cool Thoth and good thing you had a computer security specialist to help out to make it work out better. I also know why I never used Blood Sorcery for any of my players at all. All the other disciplines are more then enough to suit my characters and I could never think of a reason of why say my Malkavian would know even 1 dot of that discipline. Yes it's overthinking things out and I can't help it.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-04-2023, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}